1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,354
This video summarizes the complete Foundry lab, starting with a new
Azure resource group.

2
00:00:05,354 --> 00:00:13,354
It replays actual command and managed-service records, with long
waits removed. It is not a recording of the separately authenticated

3
00:00:13,354 --> 00:00:14,377
portal interface.

4
00:00:14,377 --> 00:00:22,618
A fictional Contoso support Agent retrieves policies, answers twelve
questions, and goes through evaluation and instruction optimization.

5
00:00:22,618 --> 00:00:25,024
This lab does not retrain model weights.

6
00:00:26,024 --> 00:00:34,123
First inspect the signed-in Azure CLI user, tenant and subscription.
A successful sign-in alone does not establish that the correct lab

7
00:00:34,123 --> 00:00:35,563
environment is selected.

8
00:00:35,563 --> 00:00:43,062
The portal and CLI authenticate separately, so check both
identities. Do not bypass personal authentication or continue under

9
00:00:43,062 --> 00:00:44,021
another account.

10
00:00:44,021 --> 00:00:51,820
Use the repository's virtual environment, set the language and
artifact directory, and repeat those settings in each new terminal.

11
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:53,740
Never mix the two language runs.

12
00:00:54,740 --> 00:01:02,251
The plan command creates local configuration and an unapproved
authorization example. Check the actual subscription, model

13
00:01:02,251 --> 00:01:05,022
selections, region and retention scope first.

14
00:01:05,022 --> 00:01:12,964
Sol serves the Agent, Luna judges the responses, and GPT five point
five handles optimization and search planning. Start with one

15
00:01:12,964 --> 00:01:17,828
hundred thousand TPM per generative deployment and ten thousand for
embeddings.

16
00:01:17,828 --> 00:01:25,955
Verify the deployed token limit rather than assuming a universal
ARM-capacity conversion. Confirm authorization before provisioning;

17
00:01:25,955 --> 00:01:28,972
a local budget entry does not stop Azure billing.

18
00:01:29,972 --> 00:01:37,718
Apply the authorized plan to create the Foundry account and project,
model deployments, Search, Application Insights and the log

19
00:01:37,718 --> 00:01:38,323
workspace.

20
00:01:38,323 --> 00:01:46,009
An accepted creation request is not full readiness. Inspect the
owned-resource status, then confirm all five runtime TPM checks

21
00:01:46,009 --> 00:01:47,582
before making model calls.

22
00:01:47,582 --> 00:01:55,207
Application Insights can add a default alert and action group.
Verify their actual relationships and default receivers without

23
00:01:55,207 --> 00:01:57,809
adopting or deleting a shared action group.

24
00:01:58,809 --> 00:02:05,048
The model smoke command checks one short, real response. This
confirms connectivity, not answer quality.

25
00:02:05,048 --> 00:02:12,727
Next upload the eight language-matched synthetic policies and
prepare the search index, knowledge base and read-only connection.

26
00:02:12,727 --> 00:02:20,347
Do not confuse creation with successful retrieval. Confirm real
references in the probe, and separately verify access under the

27
00:02:20,347 --> 00:02:25,026
Agent's managed identity rather than assuming user access proves
Agent access.

28
00:02:26,026 --> 00:02:34,439
Create the fixed version-one Agent with its policy tool. In the same
owned environment, an identical configuration should be verified and

29
00:02:34,439 --> 00:02:36,220
reused rather than recreated.

30
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:43,835
The service may return an equivalent tool-filter representation, but
changes to tools or permissions must still be rejected.

31
00:02:43,835 --> 00:02:52,002
Send the guide's example question and inspect answer, citations,
route and needs human. Verify the real policy-tool call and document

32
00:02:52,002 --> 00:02:56,178
identifiers. Valid JSON alone does not establish policy correctness.

33
00:02:57,178 --> 00:03:04,311
Use the guide's dev12 JSONL without editing it. Verify its row count
and hash, then register the first dataset version.

34
00:03:04,311 --> 00:03:12,463
A five-row preview does not mean the complete dataset has only five
items. Check all twelve in the source and in the eventual evaluation

35
00:03:12,463 --> 00:03:12,942
results.

36
00:03:12,942 --> 00:03:20,735
Query is the Agent's input. Context and ground truth are reference
material, not text to append to that input. Editing the file or

37
00:03:20,735 --> 00:03:24,331
embedding its answers in instructions breaks the comparison.

38
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:32,471
An evaluator and a Judge are different. The evaluator defines what
to score; the Judge model performs that scoring.

39
00:03:32,471 --> 00:03:40,107
Relevance passes at four or above on a five-point scale. Task
Adherence is binary: one is a pass, not a low score and not a

40
00:03:40,107 --> 00:03:41,225
threshold of four.

41
00:03:41,225 --> 00:03:49,482
Relevance uses response text, while Task Adherence receives output
items with conversation and tool context. Confirm the saved remote

42
00:03:49,482 --> 00:03:55,070
mappings and actual Judge deployment, and do not move the thresholds
after seeing results.

43
00:03:56,070 --> 00:04:04,072
After reviewing the dataset and criteria, submit the baseline once.
Steps four through six do not create three different evaluations.

44
00:04:04,072 --> 00:04:12,255
In this English run, all twelve items completed and 12 passed every
selected criterion. There were no errors or missing items, and every

45
00:04:12,255 --> 00:04:13,338
score is retained.

46
00:04:13,338 --> 00:04:21,521
Completed means processing ended, not that every answer is correct.
Use the read-only lookup to record the evaluation ID and version-one

47
00:04:21,521 --> 00:04:25,131
run ID. A long wait is not permission to submit a duplicate.

48
00:04:26,131 --> 00:04:33,486
Connect each answer and scoring reason to the source policy. An
average can hide date-boundary, citation or routing problems.

49
00:04:33,486 --> 00:04:41,253
The English run's lowest Relevance scores were four, including the
GPU-menu question. The answer correctly refused to pretend it had

50
00:04:41,253 --> 00:04:43,431
inspected the screen or live service.

51
00:04:43,431 --> 00:04:51,080
Preserve that honesty while making the supported conclusion and
verification path clearer. Check document identifiers and response

52
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:58,847
structure separately; generic evaluator passes do not certify every
business rule. Never repair the saved response to make it appear

53
00:04:58,847 --> 00:04:59,318
correct.

54
00:05:00,318 --> 00:05:08,286
In Agent Optimizer, select version one and the same dev12 dataset,
and optimize instructions only. Leave model and tool-description

55
00:05:08,286 --> 00:05:11,024
optimization off and limit candidates to two.

56
00:05:11,024 --> 00:05:19,053
Assign the optimization and evaluation models to their separate
roles, then run once. Inspect the actual instruction changes as well

57
00:05:19,053 --> 00:05:20,452
as the internal scores.

58
00:05:20,452 --> 00:05:28,177
A higher internal rank is not independent managed-evaluation
improvement or production approval. Reject changes that embed case

59
00:05:28,177 --> 00:05:32,861
answers or policy numbers, or replace honest uncertainty with
invented facts.

60
00:05:33,861 --> 00:05:41,948
Only create version two when there is a real instruction candidate
worth reviewing, and reevaluate using the baseline's exact dataset

61
00:05:41,948 --> 00:05:43,650
and evaluator configuration.

62
00:05:43,650 --> 00:05:51,555
This run selected no different instruction candidate, so it retains
version one. It does not claim that version two was created or

63
00:05:51,555 --> 00:05:54,838
reevaluated, and follows the guide's retention branch.

64
00:05:54,838 --> 00:06:03,108
For a comparison, explicitly choose version one as the baseline and
review all twelve cases. Consider nonregression, actual improvement,

65
00:06:03,108 --> 00:06:11,134
policy errors and cost tradeoffs together. Preserve inconclusive
statistics, and never repeat unchanged candidates until a favorable

66
00:06:11,134 --> 00:06:12,046
sample appears.

67
00:06:13,046 --> 00:06:21,024
The last step is not unconditional deletion. This request explicitly
retains the new resource group and its resources, so no deletion

68
00:06:21,024 --> 00:06:22,223
command is executed.

69
00:06:22,223 --> 00:06:29,661
Read the cleanup plan only, then confirm that the group still
exists. Keep the private configuration, ownership manifest and

70
00:06:29,661 --> 00:06:32,960
execution identifiers needed to reopen the environment.

71
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:40,638
Hand over shared monitoring dependencies and the possibility of
continuing Search and log charges. Closing a browser or deleting

72
00:06:40,638 --> 00:06:43,157
local records does not stop Azure billing.

73
00:06:44,157 --> 00:06:51,672
You can now reopen the created project and Agent in the retained
environment. Use the recorded names and versions rather than mixing

74
00:06:51,672 --> 00:06:53,949
results from another account or dataset.

75
00:06:53,949 --> 00:07:01,179
The point of the lab is not one high score. It is to inspect actual
answers and reasons under fixed conditions, and review only

76
00:07:01,179 --> 00:07:02,887
justified instruction changes.

77
00:07:02,887 --> 00:07:10,459
Correct procedural errors in the reusable guide without inserting
this run's verification history. This video is a separate execution

78
00:07:10,459 --> 00:07:15,583
summary; finishing the lab does not grant production approval or
guarantee future quality.
